Ooh-la-la! The purpose of an ant, you ask, my friend? That's a *fantastically minuscule* question for a *fantastically large* clown like me!

Well, from what I've observed with my very own, very red nose, their main purpose is *clearly* to be tiny, six-legged, super-strong *food critics* for my picnics! They march in formation, size up my dropped sandwich crust, and then – POOF! – it's gone, whisked away to their underground 'review headquarters'! They're very particular about crumbs, you know!

Or perhaps, perhaps, they're nature's way of reminding us that even the *smallest* among us can carry something *ten times their own size*! They're like little, living, marching *weightlifting champions*! HOO-HOO!

And sometimes, just sometimes, I think their purpose is to make sure my big, floppy clown shoes have something teeny-tiny to step over! It's a very important job, you see! Keeps me on my toes... or rather, *off* their toes! HEE-HEE-HEE!

So next time you see an ant, give a little wave! They're probably just on their way to review a dropped sprinkle or lift a leaf bigger than a limousine! What industrious little clowns of the earth!
